# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# entropy-test with no random source: the entropy PD
# finds none on transport 8 and hands out no seeds; the consumer is refused,
# finds no seed on its ring and stays not ready.
NOWAYOS: entropy: starting
NOWAYOS: entropy: no random source on transport 8: it hands out no seeds
NOWAYOS: seed-consumer: starting
NOWAYOS: seed-consumer: not ready: a draw before its first seed is refused
NOWAYOS: seed-consumer: not ready: no seed on its ring

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match),
# including in the second after the last line above: a fault, a panic, a PD
# giving up, or the consumer seeded or drawing.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!seed-consumer: seeded
!seed-consumer: drew
!seed ring 0 full
